# Q2 — Analytical Queries and Measured Outputs

## Q2 data counts

### Count notices
```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS notice_count
FROM notices;
```

Measured:
`12000`

### Count labelled pairs
```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS labelled_pairs
FROM labelled_pairs;
```

Measured:
`900`

### Label skew
```sql
SELECT label, COUNT(*) AS pair_count,
       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) / SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 2) AS percentage
FROM labelled_pairs
GROUP BY label
ORDER BY label;
```

Measured:
- different = 621 = 69%
- same = 279 = 31%

---

# Section A — Representation

## Exact Jaccard of normalized word 3-grams

```sql
SELECT
    lp.label,
    COUNT(*) AS pairs
FROM labelled_pairs lp
JOIN notice_signatures a
  ON a.notice_id = lp.notice_id_a
JOIN notice_signatures b
  ON b.notice_id = lp.notice_id_b
GROUP BY lp.label;
```

The Python measurement calculates exact Jaccard from `normalized_text`:

```text
J(A,B) = |A ∩ B| / |A ∪ B|
```

Measured normalized word 3-gram Jaccard:

SAME:
- mean 0.6354
- min 0.1920
- max 1.0000

DIFFERENT:
- mean 0.3773
- min 0.1277
- max 0.7314

---

# Section B — MinHash error

MinHash signature configuration:

```text
NUM_HASHES = 32
```

For each labelled pair:

```text
estimated_similarity =
number of equal MinHash components / 32
```

Measured:

```text
Pairs = 900
Mean absolute error = 0.0556
Maximum absolute error = 0.2515
```

Formula:

```text
MAE = mean(|estimated_similarity - exact_jaccard|)
```

---

# Section C — LSH candidate retrieval

Configuration:

```text
BANDS = 8
ROWS_PER_BAND = 4
TOTAL_HASHES = 32
```

A pair survives when at least one band produces the same bucket key.

## Labelled-pair result

```text
SAME:
204 / 279 = 73.12%

DIFFERENT:
250 / 621 = 40.26%
```

## Survival by exact similarity

```text
0.1–0.2 : 0 / 101   = 0.00%
0.2–0.3 : 1 / 148   = 0.68%
0.3–0.4 : 22 / 96   = 22.92%
0.4–0.5 : 80 / 159  = 50.31%
0.5–0.6 : 154 / 189 = 81.48%
0.6–0.7 : 82 / 92   = 89.13%
0.7–0.8 : 18 / 18   = 100.00%
0.8–0.9 : 26 / 26   = 100.00%
0.9–1.0 : 71 / 71   = 100.00%
```

